Decision: **changes requested**.

- **F1 — medium**, [review_ledger_memo.go:43](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1387710968/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_ledger_memo.go:43): concurrent callers can both miss `Load` and execute `compute` before either reaches `LoadOrStore`. Publication is synchronized; computation is not. This violates R1/R2’s “at most once” guarantee. The new tests exercise only sequential requests.
- **F2 — medium**, [review_bundle.go:3346](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1387710968/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:3346), also [review_dispatch.go:260](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1387710968/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:260): top-level copies retain nested slices and pointers. For example, changing a returned attestation’s `Criteria[0].Disposition` changes the cached attestation seen by subsequent reads and verification in that operation. Previously, reparsing isolated those objects. This violates R4; the mutation test changes only `RunID`.
- **F3 — low**, [review_bundle.go:3346](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1387710968/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:3346), also [review_dispatch.go:260](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1387710968/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:260): copying onto nil converts non-nil empty slices to nil, including without an operation. Empty attestations, coverage losses and unfiltered runs therefore change return shape; JSON serialization changes `[]` to `null`.

Applied the `pose-review` skill, review workflow, and Go, security, documentation and delivery-evidence rules. Inspected the changed implementation, tests, spec and ADR. No tests or builds were executed locally; validation conclusions below rely on the supplied sealed pipeline evidence.

The assessment commands unexpectedly modified `.pose/assessments/{integrations,technical-debt}.md` and `.pose/state/{integrations,technical-debt}.json`. Restoration was rejected by sandbox policy, so those four generated files remain modified. No implementation files were changed and no attestation was recorded.

